 		<Tag>TXT_KEY_CONCEPT_SAS_SEVOPEDIA_EVENT_TRIGGERS_LEGEND_PEDIA</Tag>
-		<English>[H1]Sevopedia Event Triggers Legend[\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]This page explains the era groupings and abbreviations used in Sevopedia Event Triggers.[PARAGRAPH:2]Era grouping:[PARAGRAPH:2]- Any era (no tech requirement): triggers that can fire from turn 1 because they declare no tech prerequisite of any kind.[PARAGRAPH:2]- Ancient / Classical / Medieval / ... : triggers whose earliest tech prerequisite is visible directly on the trigger XML, i.e. in its OrPreReqs or AndPreReqs tech list. These are "direct" era classifications - the gate is explicit on the trigger itself.[PARAGRAPH:2]- Ancient (indirect) / Classical (indirect) / ... : triggers whose era was inferred via chain lookup because the trigger XML does not list a direct tech prereq. The era comes from one of: OtherPlayerHasTech (another player must have a tech), a prerequisite event trigger's inferred era, the required Civic's prereq tech, a required Building/Unit class's default building/unit prereq tech, a required Religion's prereq tech, or a required Corporation's prereq tech. These are "indirect" - the trigger never reads "requires Flight" directly, but it requires something that implies Flight.[PARAGRAPH:2]Requirements display:[PARAGRAPH:2]- Requires (Buttons) shows linkable requirements such as techs, civics, buildings, units, religions, corporations, terrains, features, improvements, bonuses, and prerequisite event triggers.[PARAGRAPH:2]- Requires (Text) shows numeric, flag, route, target-selection, and Python-gate constraints that have no clear pedia button target.[PARAGRAPH:2]Numbered labels (numTxt) under buttons:[PARAGRAPH:2]- Oth.P. : other player has this tech. Pairs with the OtherPlayerHasTech field. This tech does not need to be researched by the trigger's player - someone else in the game must have it. The label appears because the icon art is identical to a self-prereq tech icon and would otherwise be ambiguous.[PARAGRAPH:2]- OR : appears between adjacent buttons in a Requires OR-prereq group of two or more techs, between same-field plot alternatives such as terrain/feature/improvement/bonus options, or between adjacent Obsolete with techs when multiple techs can obsolete the trigger. Means any single one satisfies that group; for Obsolete with, any single one blocks the trigger.[PARAGRAPH:2]- No connector between adjacent buttons means AND: all shown requirements apply. AND is left implicit because writing "and" between every required icon makes dense panels harder to scan.</English>
+		<English>[H1]Sevopedia Event Triggers Legend[\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]This page explains the era groupings and abbreviations used in Sevopedia Event Triggers.[PARAGRAPH:2]Era grouping:[PARAGRAPH:2]- Any era (no tech requirement): triggers that can fire from turn 1 because they declare no tech prerequisite of any kind.[PARAGRAPH:2]- Ancient / Classical / Medieval / ... : triggers whose earliest tech prerequisite is visible directly on the trigger XML, i.e. in its OrPreReqs or AndPreReqs tech list. These are "direct" era classifications - the gate is explicit on the trigger itself.[PARAGRAPH:2]- Ancient (indirect) / Classical (indirect) / ... : triggers whose era was inferred via chain lookup because the trigger XML does not list a direct tech prereq. The era comes from one of: OtherPlayerHasTech (another player must have a tech), a prerequisite event trigger's inferred era, the required Civic's prereq tech, a required Building/Unit class's default building/unit prereq tech, a required Religion's prereq tech, or a required Corporation's prereq tech. These are "indirect" - the trigger never reads "requires Flight" directly, but it requires something that implies Flight.[PARAGRAPH:2]Random event selection:[PARAGRAPH:2]- iWeight and Active in Games affect the normal automatic random-event lottery. Manual or scripted triggering can still force an event trigger outside that lottery, so iWeight 0 or Active in Games 0% does not necessarily mean the XML entry is unused.[PARAGRAPH:2]Requirements display:[PARAGRAPH:2]- Requires (Buttons) shows linkable requirements such as techs, civics, buildings, units, religions, corporations, terrains, features, improvements, bonuses, and prerequisite event triggers.[PARAGRAPH:2]- Requires (Text) shows numeric, flag, route, target-selection, and Python-gate constraints that have no clear pedia button target.[PARAGRAPH:2]Numbered labels (numTxt) under buttons:[PARAGRAPH:2]- Oth.P. : other player has this tech. Pairs with the OtherPlayerHasTech field. This tech does not need to be researched by the trigger's player - someone else in the game must have it. The label appears because the icon art is identical to a self-prereq tech icon and would otherwise be ambiguous.[PARAGRAPH:2]- OR : appears between adjacent buttons in a Requires OR-prereq group of two or more techs, between same-field plot alternatives such as terrain/feature/improvement/bonus options, or between adjacent Obsolete with techs when multiple techs can obsolete the trigger. Means any single one satisfies that group; for Obsolete with, any single one blocks the trigger.[PARAGRAPH:2]- No connector between adjacent buttons means AND: all shown requirements apply. AND is left implicit because writing "and" between every required icon makes dense panels harder to scan.</English>
